 = option A (in scope). DashScope / other hosted APIs = option B (needs separate approval).\n\n## Recommended models (candidates confirmed, not frozen forever)\n\nPrimary (dev verification + initial production):\n\n- **Qwen/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct**, Apache-2.0, Hugging Face `Qwen/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct` (checked 2026-09-19). Text + image on one model so we do not require a separate 7B/14B LLM for work-order JSON.\n- Serve with **vLLM** (or SGLang) OpenAI-compatible, **auth required**, not a naked public port.\n- Quantization: AWQ/FP8 if the chosen GPU prefers it; BF16 on 24GB is comfortable for 4B.\n\nDeferred, not simultaneous GPU residents:\n\n- Speech: **Qwen/Qwen3-ASR-0.6B** (Apache-2.0) after text/image path is live. 1.7B is the quality step-up, not the first verification.\n- Retrieval: **BAAI/bge-m3** embedding, **MIT** license per the [official model card](https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-m3) (checked 2026-09-19). Run on CPU or a second small process; reranker later (`BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3` or equivalent). Do not load VL + ASR + embedding + reranker on one 24GB card at once.\n\nPin at download (not fetched this round; no weights on disk):\n\n| Asset | Official source | License | Pin |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct | https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct | Apache-2.0 | snapshot hash recorded when download is approved |\n| Qwen3-ASR-0.6B | https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-ASR-0.6B | Apache-2.0 | snapshot hash recorded when download is approved |\n| bge-m3 | https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-m3 | MIT | snapshot hash recorded when download is approved |\n\nNot chosen now: larger Qwen3-VL-8B/32B as default (cost/VRAM without traffic evidence). Not chosen: third-party hosted Qwen APIs as the core path.\n\n## Capacity assumptions (marked as assumptions)\n\nNo real production traffic exists. Registered users �� concurrent inferences.\n\nAssumed V1 start (until real metrics exist):\n\n- 1 tenant, 1�C3 properties, 50�C200 registered accounts\n- Work-order AI: about **20 analyses/day**, peak **5 concurrent**, 1�C2k prompt tokens, 0�C3 images ��1024px\n- ASR: rare, 15�C30s clips, not on the hot path\n- Knowledge: hundreds of documents, not millions\n- Latency budget: analysis 15�C30s then human queue; provider failure must not block ticket creation\n\nA single 4B VL instance on 24GB has large headroom under these assumptions. Scale out when p95 latency or queue depth is evidenced, not when user count grows.\n\n## Where to run it\n\n**Recommend:** one operator-controlled rented GPU host (RTX 4090 24GB or equal 24GB class) in a region we manage; vLLM on that host; property backend calls it over HTTPS with a service key. Fits ��we deploy and control the weights��.\n\n**Alternative:** enterprise-owned or private-cloud 24GB+ GPU with the same compose/container, not K8s, not a rewrite of the property monolith.\n\n**Not this week without approval:** start a billed GPU; download weights onto this nearly-full D: volume; use the 5070 Ti as production.\n\n## Cost interval (estimates, not quotes)\n\nSources checked 2026-09-19: AutoDL-style listings aggregated by third-party pages (e.g. 36171.com listing Northwest 4090 **��1.98/hour**, advertised **��1100/month**; other 4090 on-demand mentions **��1.88�C3.49/hour**). Live cart price, region, spot vs reserved, and idle billing **must be confirmed before any order**. Vast.ai marketplace figures are not the default because operational control and data residency are weaker.\n\n| Mode | GPU (estimate) | Storage/network/backup/ops (estimate) | Monthly band |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Dev verification, 8�C12h/day | ��500�C1200 | ��150�C400 | **��0.7k�C1.6k** |\n| Initial production, 24/7 one 4090 | ��1100�C2500 | ��250�C600 | **��1.4k�C3.1k** |\n| Growth: second GPU when queue/SLA evidence exists | +��1100�C2500 | +��200�C500 | **+��1.3k�C3.0k** |\n\nNot included: WeChat/SMS vendor fees, Milvus disk beyond backup, engineer time, idle instances left on, model download bandwidth.\n\nSelf-host is **not** guaranteed cheaper than a hosted API at very low QPS; it is chosen for data control, migration, and long-run cost once QPS is continuous. Do **not** deploy one large model per property.\n\n## What Cursor did without new spend\n\n- Recorded inventory and this recommendation.\n- Did **not** download weights, rent a GPU, change drivers, or start an inference container.\n- Did **not** point production settings at a third-party model API.\n- Auth/identity software continued on Fake AI.\n\n## Next gated step (needs explicit approval)\n\n1. Approve **one** 24GB-class GPU rental **or** name an existing company GPU endpoint.\n2. After that: create an **isolated** inference directory/compose (not the property backend venv, not ComfyUI), download `Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct` + tokenizer/processor only, pin versions, serve with API key, run **one** structured JSON completion, then wire `LLM_BASE_URL`/`VLM_BASE_URL` in a named synthetic env.\n3. Embedding 1024-d collection is a later, separately approved schema/ops change. Auto-dispatch ORM mapping stays blocked on shared 0007 DBs.\n\nOffline-independence of the model runtime is a **model milestone**, not a login-page gate. It is **unverified** until weights exist on a target host with telemetry/download disabled for that process. Do not disconnect the whole PC, WeChat, or Cursor to fake that test.\n\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001-C\",\n  \"head_at_test\": \"8269336c259f791d4e1d115b0e5c2111c16eab46 plus uncommitted AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001-C\",\n  \"calendar\": {\n    \"work_started\": \"2026-09-15\",\n    \"operator_day5_confirmed\": \"2026-09-18\",\n    \"today\": \"2026-09-19\",\n    \"week_aim\": \"2026-09-21\"\n  },\n  \"unit\": {\n    \"command\": \"pytest tests/unit -q\",\n    \"passed\": 320,\n    \"failed\": 0,\n    \"skipped\": 0,\n    \"environment\": \"host .venv Python 3.12, no live vendors\",\n    \"note\": \"320 is this-round unit count after FIX-1. Do not cite historical 318/319 as this slice.\"\n  },\n  \"isolated_0009_runtime\": {\n    \"host_port_database\": \"127.0.0.1:3307/property_ai_auth001_test\",\n    \"alembic_revision\": \"20260919_0009\",\n    \"pytest\": [\n      \"tests/integration/test_isolated_auth_runtime.py\",\n      \"tests/integration/test_isolated_identity_runtime.py\"\n    ],\n    \"passed\": 7,\n    \"failed\": 0,\n    \"skipped\": 0,\n    \"note\": \"Prior 6 isolated auth tests plus 1 official-session bind/claim/lowercase-reset test. Not claimed as full-repo integration.\"\n  },\n  \"isolated_live_api\": {\n    \"process\": \"python scripts/ops/serve_auth001_isolated_api.py PID 46740 started 2026-09-19T10:56:05Z after passwords.py 10:54:47Z\",\n    \"base\": \"http://127.0.0.1:8083/api/v1\",\n    \"does_not_replace\": \"http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/v1\",\n    \"healthz\": 200,\n    \"schema_probe\": \"127.0.0.1:3307/property_ai_auth001_test @ 20260919_0009\"\n  },\n  \"password_policy\": {\n    \"min_length\": 8,\n    \"uppercase_required\": false,\n    \"accepted_example\": \"goodpass1\",\n    \"casefold_on_hash\": false,\n    \"login_applies_new_policy\": false\n  },\n  \"release_pack\": {\n    \"script\": \"scripts/ops/pack_miniprogram_release.py\",\n    \"inventory\": \"reports/auth-identity-ai-001/release-pack-inventory.json\",\n    \"file_count\": 79,\n    \"dev_login_files\": 0,\n    \"dev_login_registered\": false,\n    \"operator_project_config_touched\": false,\n    \"upload_submit_publish\": \"NOT_RUN\"\n  },\n  \"miniprogram_devtools\": {\n    \"status\": \"NOT_RUN_THIS_ROUND\",\n    \"ws\": \"ws://127.0.0.1:9420\",\n    \"reason\": \"port 9420 not listening\",\n    \"historical_screenshots_only\": [\"login-password.png\", \"login-sms.png\"],\n    \"password_reset_page_screenshots\": \"NOT_RUN\"\n  },\n  \"self_host_ai\": {\n    \"status\": \"PLAN_ONLY\",\n    \"running_endpoint\": false,\n    \"local_gpu_optional\": \"RTX 5070 Ti 16GB\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"reports/auth-identity-ai-001/self-host-recommendation.md\"\n  },\n  \"development_sms\": \"software-process inbox only; not real SMS acceptance\",\n  \"live_providers\": \"NOT_RUN\",\n  \"persistent_db_migrate\": \"NOT_RUN\",\n  \"not_claimed\": [\n    \"formal credential acceptance\",\n    \"real SMS\",\n    \"real WeChat\",\n    \"real AI\",\n    \"self-hosted inference running\",\n    \"offline-independent model runtime\",\n    \"miniprogram page bind/claim visual\",\n    \"Production V1\",\n    \"Day 4 PASS\"\n  ]\n}\n\n\"\"\"Official-session resident bind and employee claim on the exclusive 0009 schema.\n\nRequires AUTH_ISOLATED_DATABASE_URL. Absence is skip, not PASS.\nDoes not use Seed login, SYSTEM grants, or SQL-stamped APPROVED/ACTIVE relations.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport secrets\n\nimport pytest\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom sqlalchemy import select\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import Session, sessionmaker\n\nfrom app.core.database import create_database_engine, run_owned_transaction\nfrom app.domain.dev_seed import SEED_PERMISSIONS, SEED_ROLE_PERMISSIONS\nfrom app.main import create_app\nfrom app.model.identity import Permission, Role, RolePermission, UserRole\nfrom app.service.property import PropertyService\nfrom tests.integration.test_isolated_auth_runtime import (\n    ISOLATED_URL,\n    _error,\n    _inbox,\n    _issue,\n    _phone,\n    _send,\n    _settings,\n)\n\npytestmark = pytest.mark.skipif(\n    not ISOLATED_URL,\n    reason=(\n        \"AUTH_ISOLATED_DATABASE_URL not provisioned; \"\n        \"isolated identity runtime is not claimed as PASS\"\n    ),\n)\n\nROLE_CODES = (\"RESIDENT\", \"TENANT_ADMIN\", \"STAFF\")\nNEW_PASSWORD = \"goodpass1\"\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\ndef isolated_settings():\n    return _settings()\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\ndef isolated_client(isolated_settings):\n    with TestClient(create_app(isolated_settings)) as client:\n        yield client\n\n\ndef _auth(token: str, request_id: str) -> dict[str, str]:\n    return {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"X-Request-Id\": request_id}\n\n\ndef _items(client: TestClient, url: str, token: str, request_id: str) -> list[dict[str, object]]:\n    items: list[dict[str, object]] = []\n    after_id = 0\n    for _ in range(20):\n        response = client.get(\n            url,\n            params={\"after_id\": after_id, \"limit\": 100},\n            headers=_auth(token, request_id),\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 200, response.text\n        batch = response.json()[\"data\"][\"items\"]\n        items.extend(batch)\n        if len(batch) < 100:\n            break\n        after_id = int(batch[-1][\"id\"])\n    return items\n\n\ndef _sms_login(client: TestClient, phone: str) -> dict[str, object]:\n    challenge_id, answer = _issue(client, phone, \"login\")\n    sent = _send(client, phone, \"login\", challenge_id, answer)\n    assert sent.status_code == 200, sent.text\n    code = _inbox(client, phone, \"login\")\n    login = client.post(\n        \"/api/v1/auth/sms/login\",\n        json={\"phone\": phone, \"code\": code},\n        headers={\"X-Request-Id\": f\"login-{phone[-4:]}\"},\n    )\n    assert login.status_code == 200, login.text\n    payload = login.json()[\"data\"]\n    assert payload[\"auth_method\"] == \"sms\"\n    assert payload[\"user_id\"] > 0\n    return payload\n\n\ndef _session() -> tuple[object, Session]:\n    engine = create_database_engine(ISOLATED_URL)\n    factory = sessionmaker(\n        bind=engine,\n        class_=Session,\n        autoflush=False,\n        expire_on_commit=False,\n    )\n    return engine, factory()\n\n\ndef _ensure_rbac_catalog(session: Session) -> dict[str, Role]:\n    def _persist() -> dict[str, Role]:\n        roles: dict[str, Role] = {}\n        for code in ROLE_CODES:\n            role = session.scalar(select(Role).where(Role.code == code))\n            if role is None:\n                role = Role(code=code, name=code.replace(\"_\", \" \").title())\n                session.add(role)\n                session.flush()\n            roles[code] = role\n        permissions: dict[str, Permission] = {}\n        needed = {\n            code\n            for role_code in ROLE_CODES\n            for code in SEED_ROLE_PERMISSIONS[role_code]\n        }\n        names = {item.code: item.name for item in SEED_PERMISSIONS}\n        for code in needed:\n            permission = session.scalar(select(Permission).where(Permission.code == code))\n            if permission is None:\n                permission = Permission(code=code, name=names.get(code, code))\n                session.add(permission)\n                session.flush()\n            permissions[code] = permission\n        for role_code in ROLE_CODES:\n            for permission_code in SEED_ROLE_PERMISSIONS[role_code]:\n                existing = session.scalar(\n                    select(RolePermission).where(\n                        RolePermission.role_id == roles[role_code].id,\n                        RolePermission.permission_id == permissions[permission_code].id,\n                    )\n                )\n                if existing is None:\n                    session.add(\n                        RolePermission(\n                            role_id=roles[role_code].id,\n                            permission_id=permissions[permission_code].id,\n                        )\n                    )\n        session.flush()\n        return roles\n\n    return run_owned_transaction(session, _persist)\n\n\ndef _grant_tenant_admin(session: Session, *, user_id: int, tenant_id: int) -> None:\n    def _persist() -> None:\n        role = session.scalar(select(Role).where(Role.code == \"TENANT_ADMIN\"))\n        assert role is not None\n        existing = session.scalar(\n            select(UserRole).where(\n                UserRole.user_id == user_id,\n                UserRole.role_id == role.id,\n                UserRole.scope_type == \"TENANT\",\n                UserRole.tenant_id == tenant_id,\n                UserRole.property_id.is_(None),\n            )\n        )\n        if existing is None:\n            session.add(\n                UserRole(\n                    user_id=user_id,\n                    role_id=role.id,\n                    scope_type=\"TENANT\",\n                    tenant_id=tenant_id,\n                    property_id=None,\n                )\n            )\n            session.flush()\n\n    run_owned_transaction(session, _persist)\n\n\ndef _bootstrap_org() -> dict[str, int]:\n    engine, session = _session()\n    try:\n        suffix = secrets.token_hex(3)\n        properties = PropertyService(session)\n        tenant = properties.create_tenant(name=f\"auth001-id-tenant-{suffix}\")\n        prop = properties.create_property(\n            tenant_id=tenant.id,\n            name=f\"auth001-id-property-{suffix}\",\n            address=\"Isolated identity street\",\n        )\n        building = properties.create_building(\n            tenant_id=tenant.id,\n            property_id=prop.id,\n            code=f\"B{suffix[:4]}\",\n            name=\"Building 1\",\n        )\n        unit = properties.create_unit(\n            tenant_id=tenant.id,\n            property_id=prop.id,\n            building_id=building.id,\n            code=f\"U{suffix[:4]}\",\n            name=\"Unit 1\",\n        )\n        house = properties.create_house(\n            tenant_id=tenant.id,\n            property_id=prop.id,\n            unit_id=unit.id,\n            room_no=\"101\",\n            floor=1,\n        )\n        _ensure_rbac_catalog(session)\n        return {\n            \"tenant_id\": tenant.id,\n            \"property_id\": prop.id,\n            \"building_id\": building.id,\n            \"unit_id\": unit.id,\n            \"house_id\": house.id,\n        }\n    finally:\n        session.close()\n        engine.dispose()\n\n\ndef test_official_sessions_complete_bind_claim_and_lowercase_reset(\n    isolated_client: Tes